Mohammad Rabidul Islam, a prospective Ph.D. student for Fall 2027 in Environmental Economics at the University of Delaware, reached out to James Rising regarding his application. He detailed his academic background in applied economics, environmental policy, and renewable energy, expressing a keen interest in Rising's research on climate change and social-environmental systems. Islam inquired whether Rising would advise new students and if his background would be a suitable fit. Rising responded, acknowledging the relevance of Islam's experience but noted he would not be taking on new students for that cycle. He encouraged Islam to consider other faculty in the program with aligned research interests.
